      "content": "Course: HTML Fundamentals for Your First Webpage"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Adding Images with the img Tag"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Images are added using the <img> tag (called the image tag)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Key things to know:"
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "items": [
        "<img> does not have a closing tag",
        "It displays an image file on the page"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<img src=\"https://programiz-pro-spaces.sfo3.digitaloceanspaces.com/course-images/html-fundamentals/html-structure.png\" />"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This works, but it's incomplete."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Developers always include these attributes inside the <img> tag:"
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "items": [
        "src - the address of the image",
        "alt - text that describes what the image represents"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<img src=\"https://programiz-pro-spaces.sfo3.digitaloceanspaces.com/course-images/html-fundamentals/html-structure.png\"\n2          alt=\"Diagram showing how HTML elements form a webpage structure\"\n3        />"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
